  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Reads each candidate consumer source once and indexes all relevant N-API export references while preserving the checked inventory byte-for-byte. Also normalizes the recorded policy path, eliminating genuine Windows-only inventory drift. The audit improved from 11.2s to 1.0-1.6s on Linux and from about 28s with drift to 4.9s passing on Windows.",
    "risks": [
      "Package relevance remains intentionally specialized to the two currently audited native packages; a new native package must add its relevance rule.",
      "The broad portable tier in this isolated worktree requires native addons that were intentionally not replicated; the focused audit, architecture, and strict gates pass, and integration validation should use the primary built checkout."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integrate the two commits together and retain the focused synthetic indexing test."
    ]
  }
